// ZULRAH (OSRS, 8 January 2015). Post-2006 content, so the era rule's second half applies: it is
// ported as Old School has it, numbers off the wiki (oldschool.runescape.wiki /w/Zulrah,
// /w/Zulrah/Strategies, /w/Zul-Andra, /w/Serpentine_helm, /w/Trident_of_the_Swamp, Sept 2026) and
// art out of the OSRS cache.
//
// WHAT CAME FROM WHERE:
//   the three colours       OSRS npcs 2042/2043/2044, rendered to find out which is which
//   the stats               the cache's own array: 1 Attack, 300 Defence, 1 Strength, 500 hitpoints,
//                           300 Ranged, 300 Magic, level 725
//   the bonuses and caps    the wiki's infobox: -45 Magic defence, +50 Ranged defence, 0 melee
//                           defence, 41 max hit, 3-tick attack speed, damage taken capped at 50
//   the four rotations      the wiki's four rotation tables, phase for phase, in zulrah.enum
//   the arena               measured off the imported map square, see below
//   the drop table          the wiki's, at its own rates - scripts/zulrah_drops.rs2
//   the clouds' damage      OURS. The wiki says only "varying damage per tick which can add up
//                           quickly" and gives no number, so one was chosen and is stated here.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The shrine, and why it is on a square of its own
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Zulrah's shrine is an island in the Poison Waste lake at OSRS world x 2262-2276, z 3067-3078 -
// which crosses z = 3072, so half of it is in OSRS's m35_47 and half in m35_48. m35_48 is the
// Poison Waste this build already has and Regicide reads (the coal tar, the sulphur), and the OSRS
// map importer rewrites a whole square. So the shrine was lifted out of both squares as one 32x32
// rectangle and put down on m36_79, an empty square, by tools/importzulrahshrine.py - which is the
// same thing OSRS does with it in the end, because the fight is instanced and nobody ever stands on
// the original.
//
// The rectangle starts at local (16,16) and is four zones by four, so instance_setzone can copy it
// whole the way the Fight Cave copies its arena.
^zulrah_template = 0_36_79_16_16
^zulrah_zones = 4

// THE ARENA, as the imported square has it: a walkway shaped like a horseshoe open to the north,
// with a pool inside it. The south lobe is x24-33 z28-31, the two arms run north at x22-24 and
// x32-34, and the water between them is the pool. Everything below was measured off that, not
// remembered: the cache carries no spawn points for any of it.
//
// Where the boat puts you down - the middle of the south lobe.
^zulrah_entry = 0_36_79_28_29
// And where the return boat sits, in the water off the south lobe.
^zulrah_shrine_boat = 0_36_79_27_25

// THE FOUR PLACES ZULRAH SURFACES. The wiki's rotation tables name them middle, south, west and
// east; these are the four 5x5 blocks of open water nearest the walkway in each of those
// directions - 5x5 because that is Zulrah's size, and water because it surfaces in water and is
// moverestrict=nomove like the Kraken. A coord here is the block's southwest corner.
//
// AND "NEAREST" IS NOW TRUE OF ALL FOUR, which it was not. Measured against the imported square's
// own collision (every tile of the block water, and the shortest distance from the block to a tile
// a player can stand on): west and east sat one tile off the walkway, which is as close as a 5x5
// block of water gets before it starts overlapping the walkway itself, while middle sat at two and
// south at two. So the snake surfaced further away in two of its four places than the rule this
// file states, and further from the player than Old School puts it. Middle moves from z33 to z31
// and south from z22 to z23; west and east were already right.
^zulrah_pos_middle = 0_36_79_26_31
^zulrah_pos_south = 0_36_79_26_23
^zulrah_pos_west = 0_36_79_17_31
^zulrah_pos_east = 0_36_79_35_31
^zulrah_pos_count = 4
^zulrah_p_middle = 0
^zulrah_p_south = 1
^zulrah_p_west = 2
^zulrah_p_east = 3

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Zul-Andra
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// OSRS's m34_47, imported whole: the village existed nowhere in this build before, which is what
// quest_regicide.constant meant by "neither Arandar nor Zul-Andra appears anywhere in this cache or
// in any map file, so there is nothing to open". It does now.
//
// THE SACRIFICIAL BOAT IS IN THE MAP CACHE after all, and only once: OSRS's l34_47 places loc
// 10068 at local (38,48) shape 11 rot 1 - a varbit-4391 multi-loc whose default child is 46242,
// the Board/Quick-Board boat - and a scan of every keyed map square in the rev236 cache finds
// 10068 nowhere else in the world. The hand-placed second boat that used to sit at (31,47) has
// been taken out; see scripts/zulrah_travel.rs2 for why it was ever put there.
//
// The two priestesses ARE placed by hand: no OSRS cache holds npc spawns at all. Their tiles come
// from the OSRS wiki's own {{Map}} markers (oldschool.runescape.wiki, Sept 2026), which this round
// checked against the cache tile-for-tile before trusting them - /w/Chest_(Zul-Andra) marks
// 2196,3051 and the cache puts the deposit chest loc on exactly that tile, and /w/Sacrificial_boat
// marks 2215,3057, the centre of the 3x3 boat the cache puts at 2214,3056.
//   High Priestess Zul-Harcinqa  /w/High_Priestess_Zul-Harcinqa  x=2193 y=3056 -> local (17,48)
//   Priestess Zul-Gwenwynig      /w/Priestess_Zul-Gwenwynig      x=2212 y=3057 -> local (36,49)
// Gwenwynig goes on her tile as marked, out on the pier deck beside the boat. Harcinqa does not:
// (17,48) is where the cache puts one of the two Torches (OSRS loc 10658) that flank the dead end
// at the west of the village road, so she sits in the one free tile between them, local (17,47).
// That is the only coordinate on this square this round could not source to the tile.
// m34_47's own NPC section holds both spawns.
//
// WHERE THE BOAT PUTS YOU DOWN coming back from the shrine: the pier deck tile next to the boat,
// not the shore. The deck is walkable - its level-1 tiles carry the LINK_BELOW flag, so GameMap
// folds them onto level 0 and the level-0 "blocked" water underneath never applies.
^zulandra_dock = 0_34_47_37_48

// WHERE THE ZUL-ANDRA TELEPORT LANDS. /w/Zul-Andra calls it "centre of Zul-Andra" and
// /w/Zul-andra_teleport marks 2196,3056, which is the village road three tiles east of the High
// Priestess. THIS IS NOT HER TILE AND MUST NOT BE REUSED AS ONE: the first cut of this round used
// ^zulandra_village for both, so every player who teleported in materialised standing inside her.
// Her spawn lives in maps/m34_47.jm2, and nowhere else.
^zulandra_village = 0_34_47_20_48

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The fight
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// "Attack speed: 3 ticks (1.8 seconds)" and "Max Hit: 41" - both across all three forms. Every
// action Zulrah takes runs on that same 3-tick beat: an attack, a venom barrage and a snakeling
// orb all cost one beat, which is what the wiki's phase tables count in.
^zulrah_attackrate = 3
^zulrah_maxhit = 41
// "Damage at Zulrah is capped at 50" - per hit taken, param=max_dealt on all three records.
^zulrah_damage_cap = 50

// Submerged between phases. The cache's own animations set these: the dive is 21 frames at delay
// 2-5 (about 4 ticks) and the rise is 36 frames at delay 5 (about 6 ticks), so the snake is out of
// the fight for ten ticks between phases, which is the gap Old School leaves.
// How long the snake itself lives if nothing kills it. NOT ZERO and not small: the engine's
// DurationValid rejects anything below 1, and npc_changetype_keepall takes the same duration, so
// every colour change renews it. Five hours is past any fight; the number exists so a leaked
// instance eventually empties itself rather than holding a snake forever.
^zulrah_npc_life = 30000

^zulrah_dive_ticks = 4
^zulrah_rise_ticks = 6

// Rotations are numbered the way the wiki numbers them: 1 "Crimson A", 2 "Crimson B", 3 "Serp",
// 4 "Tanz". Which one you get is a fresh roll each fight, as it is in Old School, and the fight
// runs on past the end of a rotation into the start of the next - "Zulrah will then continue on to
// the starting phase of the next rotation".
^zulrah_rotations = 4

// The seven things Zulrah can do on a beat. The last two are the "Jad phase": one run of them
// alternates ranged and magic for its whole count, starting with whichever of the two it is named
// for, which is how the wiki states it ("10 alternating ranged/magic (starts ranged)").
^zulrah_act_range = 0
^zulrah_act_mage = 1
^zulrah_act_melee = 2
^zulrah_act_venom = 3
^zulrah_act_orb = 4
// One run that alternates the two, starting with the one it is named for - the wiki's "alternating
// 5 snakeling orbs/venom barrages" and "an alternating series of 6 venom cloud barrages and
// snakeling orbs".
^zulrah_act_alt_orb = 5
^zulrah_act_alt_venom = 6
^zulrah_act_jad_range = 7
^zulrah_act_jad_mage = 8

// THE BLUE FORM ATTACKS WITH EITHER. "Blue (Tanzanite): attacks with Ranged and Magic" - it picks
// one per attack, so this is the chance in eight that a given one is magic. Four in eight: the wiki
// gives no weighting, and an even coin is the only split it does not overstate.
^zulrah_mage_form_magic_chance = 4
^zulrah_mage_form_of = 8

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The snakelings
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// "Despite their combat level of 90, they have extremely low defence and only 1 Hitpoint" and they
// make "incredibly accurate attacks, which can hit up to 15". One hitpoint is in the npc config;
// the 15 is here because the cache cannot carry a max hit.
^zulrah_snakeling_maxhit = 15
^zulrah_snakeling_attackrate = 3
// How long a snakeling lives if nothing kills it. They also all die the moment Zulrah does - "will
// automatically die off with Zulrah when it is killed" - and when the fight is left or lost.
^zulrah_snakeling_life = 3000
// How far from the player an orb puts one down, and how far out to sweep for them when clearing up.
^zulrah_snakeling_spawn_range = 3
^zulrah_snakeling_sweep = 30

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The venom clouds
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// A barrage drops a cloud on the tile you are standing on: "If a player stands within a cloud's
// 3x3 area, they will be dealt varying damage per tick". So the cloud is 3x3 around where it lands
// and it hurts every tick you are inside it.
//
// FOUR AT A TIME. The longest barrage the wiki lists is four in a row, and a cloud outlives the
// barrage that made it, so four slots is the most that can ever be burning at once - there is no
// fifth cloud to drop on the floor.
^zulrah_cloud_slots = 4
^zulrah_cloud_radius = 1
// How long one cloud burns.
^zulrah_cloud_ticks = 25
// OURS, and the only number here that is: the wiki states no per-tick damage. One to five a tick
// for 25 ticks is up to 125 if you stand in one and do nothing, which is fatal and is meant to be,
// while a step out of it costs a few hitpoints rather than a trip.
^zulrah_cloud_maxhit = 5
// The clouds do NOT envenom - "[they] do not envenom players directly" - so nothing here touches
// the venom timer. Zulrah's own hits and the snakelings' do.

// Zulrah's own attacks envenom, at the venom that already exists in this build
// (toxic_blowpipe/scripts/venom.rs2). One hit in four, the rate the blowpipe uses.
^zulrah_venom_chance = 4

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Getting there, getting out, and dying there
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// OSRS gates Zulrah behind Regicide - you reach Zul-Andra through Tyras, and the High Priestess
// will not send anyone who has not been. Regicide IS built here (scripts/quests/quest_regicide),
// so the gate is the real one: ^regicide_complete.
//
// "Speak with High Priestess Zul-Harcinqa as sacrifice" first; after that the Priestess will row
// you. There is no fee for the crossing in Old School and there is none here.
^zulandra_volunteered = 1

// DYING AT ZULRAH. Old School does not take your items: Priestess Zul-Gwenwynig keeps them and
// hands them back. "First 50 kills: free recovery. After 50 kills: 100,000 coins per death." And
// the sting: "Any unsafe death will delete all items left inside the deathbank" - die anywhere
// else before you have collected and the lot is gone.
^zulrah_free_recoveries = 50
^zulrah_recovery_fee = 100000

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The drop table
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// "the player will also have two rolls on Zulrah's drop table, excluding tertiary items, which
// have only one roll", and separately "It's 1/256 per roll, you get two rolls per kill" for the
// uniques (Mod Ash, 26 May 2016). So a roll is: the unique table at 1/256, or else the main table
// at n/249. Everything below is the wiki's own denominator.
^zulrah_rolls = 2
^zulrah_unique_of = 256
^zulrah_unique_count = 4
^zulrah_main_of = 249
// Zulrah's scales, always, 100-299 of them - the 100% drop.
^zulrah_scales_min = 100
^zulrah_scales_max = 299
// The tertiaries, one roll a kill each.
^zulrah_elite_clue_rate = 75
^zulrah_jar_rate = 3000
^zulrah_pet_rate = 4000

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The serpentine helm
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 52 Crafting and 120 experience to chisel a visage into one; 75 Defence to wear it; 11,000 scales
// to fill it; 10 scales the moment you enter combat and 10 more every 90 ticks you stay in it,
// which is the 16 hours and 30 minutes the wiki quotes. Uncharged it keeps its penalties and loses
// everything else, and it cannot be worn at all until it holds something.
^serpentine_helm_crafting_level = 52
^serpentine_helm_crafting_xp = 1200
^serpentine_helm_level = 75
^serpentine_helm_max_charges = 11000
^serpentine_helm_charge_cost = 10
^serpentine_helm_charge_interval = 90
// Envenoming with it on: "1 in 6 chance if using a non-poisoned melee weapon; 1 in 2 if using
// poisoned weapons; 100% if using the toxic blowpipe, trident of the swamp, or toxic staff of the
// dead". The third of those is what the blowpipe and the swamp trident already do on their own.
^serpentine_helm_venom_chance = 6
^serpentine_helm_venom_chance_poisoned = 2

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The trident of the swamp
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 59 Crafting to put a magic fang on an uncharged trident, and it comes apart again. 78 Magic to
// wield, 2,500 charges, and a charge is one death rune, one chaos rune, five fire runes and one of
// Zulrah's scales - the scale where the trident of the seas takes ten coins. Max hit
// floor(Magic / 3) - 2, which is 24 at 78 and 31 at 99; the seas' is floor(Magic / 3) - 5. Four
// ticks a cast and a reach of 7, the same as the seas'.
^swamp_trident_crafting_level = 59
^swamp_trident_level = 78
^swamp_trident_max_charges = 2500
^swamp_trident_maxhit_offset = 2
